Hidden pref for the color originally black text lands on in inverted dark mode
(declined upstream as scope: https://sourceforge.net/p/skim-app/feature-requests/1777/).
Builds on 0001 (background level) and 0004 (SKPlusInvertMath): the filter's factor
and bias become per channel, so the text end can take a tint. Unset = upstream's
pure white, bit for bit.

defaults write net.sourceforge.skim-app.skim SKInvertedDarkModeTextColor -float 0.72   # light gray text
Or pick a color in Preferences > Advanced.

